    "case_id": "242",
    "case_summary": "A 76-year-old woman presented with macular edema. The patient was treated with 2 intravitreal anti–vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) injections. At 3 months after presentation, her macular edema was completely resolved, without recurrence.\n\nNo specific physical examination findings were reported in the case.\n\n- Optical Coherence Tomography Angiography (OCTA) findings:    At 6 months: No abnormality observed    At 12 months: En face OCT revealed hyperreflective tissues starting to proliferate on retinal vessels; OCTA B-scan showed pyramid-shaped proliferations    At 15 months: Hyperreflective tissues increased in size with angiogenic sprouts showing flow signals extending vertically    At 18 months: Development observed in area of preexisting proliferation    At 21 months: Enlarged horizontal structures along retina surface  - Fluorescein Angiography:    Performed at 21 months showing dendritic vascular-like structures  Image Descriptions:  Figure 1: Sequential development over 1 year showing progression from normal vessels to proliferation  Figure 2: Multimodal images at 21 months showing enlarged neovascularization",
